        "research": {
            "topic": "Namespace: turning real Macs into cloud infrastructure for developers and AI coding agents",
            "summary": "Namespace buys Apple Silicon Macs and racks them in its own data centers, renting them out as on-demand macOS compute for Xcode builds, iOS testing and CI. Because Apple's license forbids macOS on non-Apple hardware and caps VMs at two per Mac, cloud macOS can only scale by physically buying machines — and Namespace raised $23M in March 2026 to build exactly that layer for humans and coding agents.",
