            "keyPoints": [
                "macOS legally cannot be virtualized off Apple hardware — so a macOS cloud is literally a warehouse of purchased Macs.",
                "Namespace raised $23M led by NEA (with Susa Ventures and burst.vc) in March 2026 to build a compute layer for code.",
                "Its macOS fleet runs Apple M4 Pro and M5 Max silicon, with Xcode, iOS simulators and Metal supported natively.",
                "Cognition's Devin runs autonomous iOS builds on Namespace macOS Devboxes powered by Apple M5 — Namespace is the only Outposts provider offering macOS.",
                "Customers include fal.ai, LiveKit, Zed, Framer, Vanta and Verkada; Buildkite Hosted Agents and Warp Background Agents build on it.",
                "Apple's two-VM-per-Mac cap means scaling this cloud is a hardware purchasing problem, not a software one.",
                "Apple refreshed the Mac mini (M6, from $899) and Mac Studio (M5 Ultra, from $5,499) on August 25, 2026 — the same boxes these fleets are built from."
            ],
