            "title": "Namespace Turns Real Macs Into Cloud Servers",
            "description": "Namespace is buying Macs at scale and racking them in its own data centers, turning Apple Silicon into cloud infrastructure developers can rent. That means on-demand capacity for Xcode builds, iOS testing, and CI — plus remote macOS environments where AI coding agents can build and test Apple apps on their own. It's a glimpse at what cloud infrastructure might look like next.",
